{"title":"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three players, Ava, Beau, and Cato, are playing a tournament. Each person plays exactly two games, one game against each of the other players. If a game ends in a tie, both players are awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point. Otherwise, the winning player is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> points and the losing player is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points.\n</p><p>For example, if the tournament results are as shown below and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129a394e53ae5d9485467a5da722ed2d61c63077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = 2$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, then points are awarded as follows:\n</p><p>(add a table to the Problem 2 page)\n</p><p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to the sum of the points that have been awarded to the three players when the tournament has finished. In the example above, Ava is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point, Beau is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, and Cato is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae948412b3206828fd197dbd41fd8a41bf7c4de5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> in the example.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the tournament finishes with exactly one of the three games ending in a tie. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/4/24468ae0baa4e779a1f7de485331e5dc0ce74b02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people are involved in each game and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point is awarded to each person in a tied game, each tied game increases the total number of points by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d34a068fc593714a83c298e0e3570977270c1c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />. We also see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/647b24699730c2a6dbe787f5052e16f0e0149d69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W + 0 = W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" /> points are added to the total for every game where one person wins and the other loses from the rules.\n</p><p>We also can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> game being tied means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> games had one winner and one loser, and we know that the total number of points in this specific tournament is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/4/24468ae0baa4e779a1f7de485331e5dc0ce74b02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/7609616d1431a17d9e53bc677670b027cc6dcc7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2W + 2 \\times 1 = 2W + 2 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"220\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/2/6d21c8da41738a686b0073f4e278e30dfb1a6258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2W = 24 - 2 = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b33eb1b9bc42ccf3ab7fed5beb70d868d71efd53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = \\frac{22}{2} = \\boxed{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018031929\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.018 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 77/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1050/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3677/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.797      1 2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    8.797      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35038:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018031929 and revision id 272002. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}